WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:03.160
Your goal is

2
00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:05.180
fifteen percent more orders by March,

3
00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:06.780
at the same cost per order.

4
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.340
That is a good goal.

5
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.020
But how will you know you bought it?

6
00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:15.400
Here are four principles, before we plan anything.

7
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:21.360
Principle one is to measure whether the goals were met,

8
00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:22.780
and not only to act.

9
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:24.860
Activity is not evidence.

10
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:26.560
If you cannot name the number

11
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:27.700
that proves a goal happened,

12
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.260
it was an aspiration.

13
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.180
Principle two is that measurement starts tactical and intuitive,

14
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.380
and then matures into precise insight.

15
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.760
Nobody's first dashboard is right.

16
00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.220
So start measuring badly rather than not at all,

17
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.760
and sharpen it every month.

18
00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.140
Principle three is to understand what works,

19
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:54.060
what does not,

20
00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:55.320
which campaign failed,

21
00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.320
and which investment was profitable.

22
00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.360
You need all four, not just the first.

23
00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.600
A plan that only reports successes

24
00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.200
cannot be optimised.

25
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.520
Principle four is that building the measurement infrastructure

26
00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.080
is a necessary step

27
00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.120
before any marketing activity begins.

28
00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:14.820
Set it up before the campaign,

29
00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.600
because nobody sets up tracking retroactively.

30
00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.660
Data you do not collect today

31
00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:21.740
cannot be analysed in the future.

32
00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.500
So before you spend anything,

33
00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:27.960
the tracking goes in.

34
00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.520
Now open your workbook and write your goal,

35
00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:32.980
and how and from when you will measure it.

